Z||000000||fierocritter||11-12-2001||10:11 PM||||Was driving my 85 Fiero Gt home and it Quit, no warning, no engine light, half a tank of fuel. After diagnosing that night after it was towed home it had no spark. Two thosand miles earlier the coil and the ignition module was replaced along with the wires and plugs. The next mourning I got up to find out what was going on and it started right up. been running fine ever since. Wiggled all wiring and harnesses. I don't have a clue? Thought maybe pick-up coil but was told when it goes it does not come back. Also have another problem. Anytime I refuel my car runs like crap for about the first minute, only when I refuel. Some times will actually backfire. There is no acceleration and sometimes will even stall. Any help on either problem is a help. By the way I only run on 94 octane. Thanx.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Gary W||11-12-2001||10:40 PM||||Pickup coils can fail when hot. You could also have a bad ignition module. You did use an AC Delco one, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Your fueling problem sounds like you're stirring up crap or water in the tank when you fill up. Try running some dry-gas through a couple of tanks. Octane rating has no bearing on fuel quality. Unless your engine is designed for high-octane fuel, you're just spending money for nothing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierocritter||11-12-2001||11:02 PM||||Thanks for the reply. It very well could be the problem with the gas, never thought of that. Just replaced fuel filter about 2,000 miles ago. will try dry gas. The other problem I don"t think it is the coil. When it iniatially quit the car wasn't up to operating temp. Now when I started it after the problem i let it get hot and nothing happen. I don't know what to do know? I don"t dare trust it!||||reg||1
